  "prefLabel": "Mec 701.02 Scope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 701.02 Scope.\n\n(a) These rules shall establish a voluntary heating installers and heating equipment service personnel certification program for the following:\n\n(1) Individuals involved in the installation of residential and non-residential heating equipment systems, water heating systems, or appliances using heating oil; and\n\n(2) Individuals involved in the servicing and repair of heating equipment, water heating systems, or appliances using heating oil.\n\n(b) No person shall hold him or herself out as a certified heating installer or heating equipment service personnel unless the certification was obtained pursuant to these rules.\n\n(c) No person less than 18 years of age shall be issued a certificate pursuant to these rules.\n\n(d) Any person certified as a heating installer or heating equipment service personnel pursuant to these rules shall be deemed a qualified person as defined in NFPA 31, Standard for the Installation of Oil Burner Equipment, as adopted in the State Fire Code.\n\nSource. #13631, eff 7-9-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec700.html"
